y":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Problem\n\n`'completefuzzycollect'` prevents `i_CTRL-X_CTRL-N` from completing next word in *master* branch.\n\n😺 Thanks for all of your hard work. This just a low-priority bug for a recently added option that I wanted to bring to your attention. I don't need to use this option.\n\nWhile filling out the rest, I realized it's a vim9.1.1178 bug. This opt was inherited and it causes i_CTRL-X_CTRL-N to malfunction. Close if desired.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```sh\nwget https://github.com/neovim/neovim/releases/download/nightly/nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage\nchmod u+x nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage\n./nvim-linux-x86_64.appimage --appimage-extract\n./squashfs-root/usr/bin/nvim -u NONE\n```\n```vim\n:set completefuzzycollect=keyword\n:put=['hello world foo bar','']\n```\ntype \"hello\", <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>x</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>n</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>x</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>n</kbd>\n\nNote: it doesn't complete \" world\".\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThis does work:\n\n```vim\n:set completefuzzycollect=\n```\ntype <kbd>Esc</kbd>, <kbd>c</kbd><kbd>c</kbd>, \"hello\", <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>x</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>n</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>x</kbd>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>n</kbd>\n\nNote: it completes \" world\".\n\nThat's how I would expect it to work.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/b756a6165a06a1bca018a30dfa6b6394dc5f1208\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes 9.1.1734\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narchlinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nst\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nst-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nmaster, aur nightly","closed_by":{"login":"zeertzjq","id":35768171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzY4MTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35768171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq","html_url":"https://github.com/zeertzjq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq/followers","f